# Every text file is LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This machine is Windows, CI is Linux, and the tree is LF today. Without this file a
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every line ending, and the first diff
# after that would touch every file in the project. It would also change the bytes of
# index.html — app/security/csp.py normalises CRLF before hashing precisely because that has
# bitten projects before, but the normalisation is a backstop, not a reason to allow it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to diff or convert them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary

# 166,241 generated lines. Marked so diffs and language statistics skip it; regenerate it
# with api/tools/build_password_list.py rather than editing it.
api/app/security/data/common_passwords.txt linguist-generated=true -diff
api/requirements.lock      linguist-generated=true
api/requirements-dev.lock  linguist-generated=true
